<title>GERMANY: Buba says sells 3.0 bln marks of new 30-year bond.</title>
<headline>Buba says sells 3.0 bln marks of new 30-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank said on Tuesday that it had sold 3.0 billion marks of the Bonn government's new 6.5 percent coupon 30-year bond via a consortium of banks.</p>
<p>The bond, sold at 99.75, had a yield of 6.52 percent, the Bundesbank said.</p>
<p>The paper matures on July 4, 2027.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
